## paper.pdf SHA256
Not present in `../artifacts/`. PDF was not needed because JATS XML was available and
semantically richer. If a PDF sha256 is required for a future audit, the canonical download
URL is above (needs a real browser or authenticated user agent — headless `curl` gets 403).

## Reproducer if a Nougat parse is later desired
```bash
# 1. Fetch PDF via authenticated browser (403s to curl); save to artifacts/paper.pdf
# 2. Then, on a GPU node with nougat installed:
nougat artifacts/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base --recompute
# Output: extraction/paper.mmd
```
This is not on the critical path for reproducing the model, but would be useful if the
paper's figure numeric values (Figs. 3-5) need to be re-derived from any embedded raster
data.

## Downstream dependency: Krisko & Radman 2010 PNAS
The single blocker for a full quantitative replication is *not* this paper's PDF; it is the
Krisko & Radman (2010) *PNAS* 107:14373 figure data (F(D) carbonylation and S(D) survival
curves). That paper has no tabular SI, and its figure binaries return reCAPTCHA HTML on
headless PMC/EuropePMC fetches. WebPlotDigitizer on those figures in an interactive
browser is the unblocked path forward. See `../report/workflow.md` and
`../report/failure_analysis.md`.
